xvTMZXe5thCmaV2vqxx9oYv5-3yYPkxck4eqnLStvAPCTyO7quhCnJXRiOsA-7og5MxlPCBzZqRdaeLfvhdEGSZkXqbf2i14Vr2O_TGizEzihVRuR06Cn_B-X_YIGggPmiBOon7jx8o87FwNqmN8m2IdTGfmhIx5HTNRMaMfg3QAh3ZyO_nFMJeH6xZ2D9j__-H1xVQJCTQwAA","summary":{"white":"Mukhammadzokhid Suyarov","black":"Artem Uskov","whiteElo":"2576","blackElo":"2545","result":"1-0","opening":"Queen's Pawn Game: London System","as":"w","accuracy":{"w":89.4,"b":83},"counts":{"w":{"best":15,"great":2,"brilliant":1},"b":{"best":14,"great":1,"blunder":1}},"moment":{"name":"32.Nxg6","cls":"brilliant","color":"w","fen":"1r1r4/1p3qk1/p1bb1pNp/3p4/3P2P1/P1N1R3/1PQ2PP1/4R1K1 b - - 0 32","from":"h4","to":"g6"},"finalFen":"4rb2/1p5k/p1b2p2/3p1N1q/3P1Q2/P1N4R/1P3PP1/6K1 b - - 1 41"},"white":"Mukhammadzokhid Suyarov","black":"Artem Uskov","labels":["book","book","book","book","book","book","book","book","book","book","book","book","book","book","book","book","book","book","best","excellent","good","good","good","inaccuracy","inaccuracy","best","best","excellent","best","excellent","good","best","best","best","excellent","good","good","best","best","good","best","excellent","inaccuracy","excellent","best","best","best","best","best","great","best","best","excellent","good","best","good","best","inaccuracy","good","blunder","great","best","brilliant","best","great","best","excellent","best","good","good","best","best","best","best","excellent","best","good","inaccuracy","excellent","inaccuracy","best"],"moments":[{"ply":50,"name":"25…Nd5","cls":"great","color":"b","headline":"25…Nd5! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["The next best move, 25…Rhe8, would drop Black's winning chances from 48% to 32% (+2.03).","25…Nd5 threatens …Nxe3, winning the exchange, and stops Bxe6.","It threatens …Nxe3, winning the exchange, so White has to spend the next move on it.","White was threatening Bxe6, winning a pawn. Nd5 takes care of it.","The engine's plan continues with …Bc6 and …Qd8: this move is the first step.","White answers 26.Bxd5, taking the knight on d5, leaving Black with an isolated pawn on d5."]},{"ply":60,"name":"30…Qc7","cls":"blunder","color":"b","headline":"30…Qc7 is a blunder: Black's winning chances go from 39% to 17%.","points":["White answers 31.Qc2: adds a decisive attacker on the g6 pawn: 2 attackers against 1 defender.","After Qc2, White wins 1 point of material within 4 moves.","Better was 30…Be8 (+1.24): shores up the g6 pawn, which was under as much attack as it had defence (1 against 1)."],"better":"30…Be8 shores up the g6 pawn. After 31.Qc2 Bf7 32.Re7 Bxe7 33.Rxe7 Kf8 34.Rxf7+ Kxf7 35.Qxg6+ Ke6, Black comes out a piece up (+1.24)."},{"ply":61,"name":"31.Qc2","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"31.Qc2! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Adds a decisive attacker on the g6 pawn: 2 attackers against 1 defender.","The queen aims at the g6 pawn, a weak point in front of the Black king.","The next best move, 31.Qd1, would drop White's winning chances from 83% to 52% (+0.22).","31.Qc2 wins a pawn, picking it up with 32.Nxg6, and threatens Qxg6+, winning a pawn.","Sets up a sequence and wins a pawn once the captures settle, picking it up with 32.Nxg6.","It threatens Qxg6+, winning a pawn, so Black has to spend the next move on it."]},{"ply":63,"name":"32.Nxg6","cls":"brilliant","color":"w","headline":"32.Nxg6!! A real sacrifice: White gives up material and the engine still rates it best.","points":["Puts the knight on g6 where it can be taken.","Taking is too dangerous: Black's best reply is 32…Re8 33.Nh4 Bf8 34.Nf5+ instead (the engine rates it +4.28).","Takes the pawn on g6.","Leaves Black with an isolated pawn on f6: a long-term weakness.","32.Nxg6 wins a pawn and threatens Re7, winning the queen for a rook, picking it up with 33.Rxf7+.","Takes the g6 pawn and wins a pawn once the captures settle."],"why":[{"title":"The idea","text":"32.Nxg6!! offers the knight on g6. Taking it gives White the material back and more."},{"title":"What White gives up","text":"32.Nxg6 puts the knight on g6 where it can be taken by the queen on f7. That's a knight on offer."},{"title":"If Black takes the knight","text":"32…Qxg6 is met by 33.Re7+. Then 34.Rxe7+ gives check, and 35.Rxf7+ gives check. Material is level and White is winning (+5.79)."},{"title":"Black's best try","text":"Black's best is to leave the knight alone and play 32…Re8. White answers 33.Nh4, and the knight on g6 gets away, threatening Nf5+, winning a bishop. Then 34.Nf5+ gives check, and 37.Rxe3 takes the rook on e3. White ends up 6 points of material ahead: White is winning (+4.28)."},{"title":"Without the sacrifice","text":"The best move without the sacrifice, 32.g3, is clearly weaker (+0.14 against +4.28). Black answers 32…Re8, taking the open e-file, aiming at the rook on e3. That would leave White level."}]},{"ply":65,"name":"33.Nh4","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"33.Nh4! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["The next best move, 33.Ne7, would drop White's winning chances from 81% to 17% (−4.39).","33.Nh4 gets the knight out of the way of …Qxg6 and threatens Nf5+, winning a bishop, picking it up with 34.Nxd6.","Black was threatening …Qxg6, winning a knight. The knight steps away.","It threatens Nf5+, winning a bishop, picking it up with 34.Nxd6, so Black has to spend the next move on it.","The engine's plan continues with Qd1 and Nf5+: this move is the first step.","Black answers 33…Bf8, winning a rook."]}],"opening":{"name":"Queen's Pawn Game: London System","eco":"D02","points":["Both sides followed opening theory up to 9…Ng7: 18 moves in all, 9 by White and 9 by Black.","Theory runs out after 9…Ng7: too few games between strong players reached this position to go further."]}}